h(2, id: "footnotes") { 14. Footnotes }

p {
    A definition is a top-level block. A reference is an inline.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
p { See the rule.fn(required-title) }

footnote(id: "required-title") { Title is required when meta is present. }
!}

p {
    The definition needs a non-empty code{id} attribute. The body is prose.
}

p {
    The reference is code{fn(id)} or a quoted string inside the parentheses. The
    identifier form allows letters, digits, underscore, and hyphen.
}

p {
    Checks:
}

list {
    item { Duplicate definition ids are a semantic error. }
    item { A reference whose id has no definition is a semantic error. }
    item {
        Definitions with no references still appear in the footnotes section.
    }
}

p {
    Numbering follows first-reference order in the document after includes are
    merged. Definitions that were never referenced are appended after that list.
    Output ids are code{fn-} plus the id, and code{fnref-} plus the id.
}

p {
    This page uses four definitions. Earlier sections reference the first
    three.fn("include-meta")
}
